@page "/api"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "API";
}
<div class="docs-layout shell">
    <aside class="sidebar" aria-label="API navigation">
        <p class="sidebar-title">API</p>
        <a href="#overview" aria-current="page">Overview</a>
        <span>Authentication <small>Coming soon</small></span>
        <span>Endpoints <small>Coming soon</small></span>
        <span>Errors <small>Coming soon</small></span>
    </aside>
    <article class="docs-content" id="overview">
        <p class="eyebrow">DEVELOPER DOCUMENTATION</p>
        <h1>PocketLedger API</h1>
        <p class="lead">The API documentation will cover authentication, request and response formats, endpoints and practical examples for client developers.</p>
        <div class="notice">
            <strong>The API reference is not published yet.</strong>
            <p>Endpoint details and executable examples will be added once the public API contract is documented.</p>
        </div>
        <h2>Example format</h2>
        <p>Examples will be ready to copy and will clearly mark the values that need to be replaced.</p>
        <div class="code-block">
            <button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy-code aria-live="polite">Copy</button>
            <pre aria-label="Placeholder curl example"><code>curl https://api.example.com/resource \
  --header "Authorization: Bearer &lt;access-token&gt;"</code></pre>
        </div>
        <h2>Planned topics</h2>
        <ul class="topic-list">
            <li><strong>Authentication</strong><span>Obtain and use access tokens safely.</span></li>
            <li><strong>API conventions</strong><span>Understand formats, pagination, validation and errors.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Endpoint reference</strong><span>See inputs, outputs and copyable curl requests.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Client integration</strong><span>Follow a practical path from the first request to a working client.</span></li>
        </ul>
    </article>
</div>
